      "tag": "Formation",
      "h2": "Using ΔHf values",
      "body_html": "<p>For aA + bB -> cC + dD: ΔHr = (c×ΔHf C + d×ΔHf D) - (a×ΔHf A + b×ΔHf B).</p><p>Set ΔHf of elements in standard states to zero.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Combustion",
      "h2": "Using ΔHc values",
      "body_html": "<p>ΔHr = Σ ΔHc(reactants) - Σ ΔHc(products). Apply when ΔHc data is given.</p><p>Useful for forming hydrocarbons from elements where direct route is impractical.</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Worked",
      "h2": "Worked example",
      "body_html": "<p>Find ΔHr for CH4 + 2O2 -> CO2 + 2H2O. Use ΔHf: CO2 = -394, H2O = -286, CH4 = -75.</p><p>ΔHr = (-394 + 2×-286) - (-75 + 0) = -966 + 75 = -891 kJ/mol.</p>"
    }
